scale(x, i) returns x * radix(x)**i.

default real examples:
x = -3.5
  scale(x,  1) = -7.0
  scale(x, -1) = -1.75
  scale(x,  2) = -14.0
x = -1.0
  scale(x,  1) = -2.0
  scale(x, -1) = -0.5
  scale(x,  2) = -4.0
x = -0.5
  scale(x,  1) = -1.0
  scale(x, -1) = -0.25
  scale(x,  2) = -2.0
x = 0.0
  scale(x,  1) = 0.0
  scale(x, -1) = 0.0
  scale(x,  2) = 0.0
x = 0.5
  scale(x,  1) = 1.0
  scale(x, -1) = 0.25
  scale(x,  2) = 2.0
x = 1.0
  scale(x,  1) = 2.0
  scale(x, -1) = 0.5
  scale(x,  2) = 4.0
x = 3.5
  scale(x,  1) = 7.0
  scale(x, -1) = 1.75
  scale(x,  2) = 14.0

kind examples:
scale(1.5,   3) = 12.0
scale(1.5_4, 3) = 12.0
scale(1.5_8, 3) = 12.0

using exponent:
x = -3.5  exponent(x) = 2  scale(fraction(x), exponent(x)) = -3.5
x = -1.0  exponent(x) = 1  scale(fraction(x), exponent(x)) = -1.0
x = -0.5  exponent(x) = 0  scale(fraction(x), exponent(x)) = -0.5
x = 0.5  exponent(x) = 0  scale(fraction(x), exponent(x)) = 0.5
x = 1.0  exponent(x) = 1  scale(fraction(x), exponent(x)) = 1.0
x = 3.5  exponent(x) = 2  scale(fraction(x), exponent(x)) = 3.5
